  "notes": [
    "Offer A has a 3% fee ($180), 0% introductory APR and 24% later APR. Its introductory duration and monthly budget change only where the row says so. The other path is a 24% original card unless the row explicitly compares offer B.",
    "The two-offer row uses $250 monthly for both paths. Offer B has a 5% fee ($300), 0% APR for 24 months and 24% afterward. A larger fee and longer promotion can trade off differently at a different repayment budget.",
    "A financed fee is added once to the initial balance. Paying it separately requires $180 at transfer in addition to the monthly budget. The upfront-fee row therefore does not use equal initial cash. Borrowing cost counts the fee once plus modeled interest.",
    "The subsequent APR starts in the month after the promotional period on the remaining balance. This is not deferred interest charged retroactively. Payments are capped at the final amount owed; fractional cents are retained.",
    "The payment needed to clear a promotional balance is a payoff-plan amount, not the contractual minimum. This monthly model excludes new purchases, credit-limit eligibility, missed payments, annual fees and issuer-specific daily balance conventions."
